{"author":"rebar-bridge[bot]","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1794264639989213002,"compiled_state":{"alias":"volcanic-prim-parakeet","assignee":null,"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":4,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"057827798b8103b5279f1e699823c9a652aa49fc2849feb36daa3c3ac288b9b5","event_uuid":"dbc3eb68-9072-441b-9a8f-6407b96a369d","position":{"commit_sha":"2a519849c22e854031a06b0955c192b1ea55bc99","position":"1794256428415492001-dbc3eb68-9072-441b-9a8f-6407b96a369d"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIGNNmnI/WYNJAOKH9yvo0l+tMYJR2tK2UV4H8ReXBQU5 rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com rotated-20260907"},{"content_hash":"9320b9fde0a297a909ddfb29759ccc988f24cfe9f3dca94ff76e20e929c7a355","event_uuid":"7049910d-7866-43ec-a945-b38d2e0aaee5","position":{"commit_sha":"6b7f2566c91e428c1924009483fdc2c0dfd41aef","position":"1794256652589014001-7049910d-7866-43ec-a945-b38d2e0aaee5"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIGNNmnI/WYNJAOKH9yvo0l+tMYJR2tK2UV4H8ReXBQU5 rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com rotated-20260907"},{"content_hash":"5a1f80cf7186d04a52f21cf86bf13ecc70625e03f6a4b6a59ea62d86d9a747bd","event_uuid":"cbf22e23-2298-4d3d-adc0-816130ac80e7","position":{"commit_sha":"a79421d99aba7a4dea15d0f55cb899393e0712e2","position":"1794256793074106001-cbf22e23-2298-4d3d-adc0-816130ac80e7"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIGNNmnI/WYNJAOKH9yvo0l+tMYJR2tK2UV4H8ReXBQU5 rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com rotated-20260907"},{"content_hash":"f3aa68dafd05524ef278f527c64278911e0000869142efc876ff799ccf6be64e","event_uuid":"b05d584d-ca72-4975-a9a8-b9ee519cb164","position":{"commit_sha":"a8b941f0796e5f5ece3bf3c66db5ff3da94eaf1d","position":"1794264639989213001-b05d584d-ca72-4975-a9a8-b9ee519cb164"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIGNNmnI/WYNJAOKH9yvo0l+tMYJR2tK2UV4H8ReXBQU5 rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com rotated-20260907"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1794256428415492001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"cbf22e23-2298-4d3d-adc0-816130ac80e7","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"50aa-b7a1-e9a1-44ac"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nAfter the inbound child, Jira fix versions reach rebar but a release set on a rebar ticket never reaches Jira: no outbound differ compares `releases`, and neither transport has a fix-version write. The epic requires both directions. This child implements rebar→Jira as designed in ADR 0124 (decisions 5 and 6), following the tags→labels path, so the epic's round-trip criterion holds for both Jira adapters.\n\n## Approach\n\n1. **Transport verbs.** Add `add_fix_version(remote_id, name)` and `remove_fix_version(remote_id, name)` to the `TicketTransport` protocol in `src/rebar/reconciler/_backend.py`, beside `add_label`/`remove_label` (lines 171 and 216), and implement them per adapter with per-item update verbs only (never a whole-list `set`, so a concurrent Jira-side edit survives):\n   - Cloud, in `src/rebar/reconciler/adapters/jira/acli_graph.py` next to `add_label` (line 137): `self._direct_rest_put_raw(f\"/rest/api/3/issue/{key}\", {\"update\": {\"fixVersions\": [{\"add\": {\"name\": name}}]}})`, and `remove` likewise. `_direct_rest_put_raw` (`acli_rest.py:118-141`) raises `HTTPError` on non-2xx, which is the failure signal (ACLI is bypassed, as for parent and priority).\n   - Data Center, in `src/rebar/reconciler/adapters/jira_datacenter/_issues.py` next to `remove_label` (lines 182-197): `issue.update(update={\"fixVersions\": [{\"add\": {\"name\": name}}]})` through `_with_connection_retry`, the verb the DC label remove already uses.\n   Atlassian documents Fix Versions as accepting Set, Add and Remove by version id or name (ADR 0124 Evidence); the live write is first exercised by the production-verification child, because no Jira project on the site has a version.\n2. **Intent set.** In `src/rebar/reconciler/local_label_intent.py`, generalize the event scan so it can collect a second field: add `compute_release_intent_map(bound_local_ids, tracker_dir)` that gathers names from non-inbound `RELEASE_DELTA.added` and `SNAPSHOT.compiled_state.releases`, skipping `source == \"inbound\"` events exactly as the tag scan does (lines 68-80, bug a06c). Compute it in `outbound_pass.py` next to `compute_label_intent_map` (line 91) and pass it as a new `local_release_intent` on `OutboundDiffConfig` (`outbound_differ.py`, beside `local_label_intent` at line 184).\n3. **Diff.** New module `src/rebar/reconciler/outbound_releases.py` with `_diff_releases(ticket, jira_fields, intent_set)`: ADD each local name missing from the issue's `fixVersions` names; REMOVE an issue name missing locally only when it is in `intent_set` (a name Jira added and rebar never held is never removed); return `[]` when `fixVersions` is unobserved. Records are `{\"action\": ..., \"release\": name}`. A new sibling module, like `outbound_labels`/`outbound_links`, keeps `outbound_differ.py` (466 lines) and `outbound_mutation_builders.py` (327 lines) from growing a second inline collection diff.\n4. **Mutation.** Add `releases` to `OutboundMutation` (`outbound_differ.py:157`) and to `OutboundUpdatePayload`, `_OUTBOUND_UPDATE_KEYS` and its non-empty check (`mutation_payloads.py:128-170`). Call `_diff_releases` in the bound-update builder (`outbound_mutation_builders.py:270-277`) and include `releases` in the emit condition and the `RECON: outbound_update` log line (lines 306-316). If that raises the builder's complexity above its ceiling, extract the existing label+annotation block (lines 270-294) into a helper first, behavior-preserving.\n5. **Dispatch.** Add `_update_one_dispatch_releases(mutation, client, issue_key)` in `src/rebar/reconciler/dispatch_one.py`, mirroring `_update_one_dispatch_labels` (lines 520-546): best-effort per item, a failure logged to stderr and retried next pass, computed/applied counts returned. Call it beside the labels call (line 333).\n6. **Same-pass suppression.** In `inbound_differ._build_outbound_context` (lines 186-231) record `release_adds`/`release_removes`, and apply the `_suppress_collection_echoes` helper from the inbound child to release mutations, so an outbound ADD drops the inbound REMOVE of the same name and vice versa.\n7. **Create path.** A new Jira issue created from a rebar ticket gets its releases on the next pass through the bound-update diff; the create payload is unchanged.\n8. **Contract property.** Extend `tests/unit/reconciler/test_field_contract_properties.py` with the intent gate: a name on the Jira issue that is not in the intent set is never removed.\n9. **Docs.** Mark the outbound cell of the fix-versions row in `docs/jira-sync-setup.md` as supported, and state that writes use per-item add/remove.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/reconciler/_backend.py`\n- `src/rebar/reconciler/adapters/jira/acli_graph.py`\n- `src/rebar/reconciler/adapters/jira_datacenter/_issues.py`\n- `src/rebar/reconciler/local_label_intent.py`\n- `src/rebar/reconciler/outbound_releases.py` (new)\n- `src/rebar/reconciler/outbound_differ.py`\n- `src/rebar/reconciler/outbound_mutation_builders.py`\n- `src/rebar/reconciler/outbound_pass.py`\n- `src/rebar/reconciler/mutation_payloads.py`\n- `src/rebar/reconciler/dispatch_one.py`\n- `src/rebar/reconciler/inbound_differ.py`\n- `docs/jira-sync-setup.md`\n- `tests/unit/reconciler/diffing/test_outbound_releases.py` (new)\n- `tests/unit/reconciler/mutate/test_fix_version_transport.py` (new)\n- `tests/unit/reconciler/mutate/test_local_label_intent.py` (extend)\n- `tests/unit/reconciler/test_field_contract_properties.py` (extend)\n- `tests/integration/reconciler/test_reconcile_releases_roundtrip.py` (new)\n\n## Testing\n\n- Transport: Cloud `add_fix_version(\"REB-1\",\"2.4\")` issues `PUT /rest/api/3/issue/REB-1` with body `{\"update\":{\"fixVersions\":[{\"add\":{\"name\":\"2.4\"}}]}}` (captured `urllib` request); `remove` sends `{\"remove\":{\"name\":\"2.4\"}}`; a 400 raises `HTTPError`. DC calls `issue.update(update={\"fixVersions\":[{\"add\":{\"name\":\"2.4\"}}]})` on a fake pycontribs issue. Neither path ever sends `set` or `fields.fixVersions`.\n- Diff: local `[\"2.4\"]`, Jira `[]` yields add `2.4`; local `[]`, Jira `[\"2.4\"]` with `2.4` in intent yields remove, without it yields `[]`; unobserved `fixVersions` yields `[]`.\n- Intent: a `RELEASE_DELTA` with `source=\"inbound\"` contributes nothing; a local one and a `SNAPSHOT` with `releases` contribute their names.\n- Suppression: an outbound ADD of `2.4` drops the inbound REMOVE of `2.4` in the same pass.\n- Round trip (integration tier, both a Cloud-shaped and a DC-shaped fake transport): pass 1 with a local release pushes one add; pass 2 with Jira reflecting it writes nothing on either side; a Jira-side add of a new name arrives as one `RELEASE_DELTA`; pass 3 writes nothing.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] A release added or removed on a bound rebar ticket produces exactly one per-item `fixVersions` add or remove on the Jira issue in the next pass, on both the Cloud and DC transports, and the payloads match the bodies above; pinned by the transport and round-trip tests.\n- [ ] A Jira fix version that rebar never held is never removed by the bridge; pinned by the diff test and the contract property test.\n- [ ] A repeat pass with no change on either side writes no Jira update and no rebar event, for both adapter shapes; pinned by the round-trip test.\n- [ ] Same-pass outbound release changes suppress the opposing inbound change; pinned by the suppression test.\n- [ ] Existing label outbound and dispatch tests pass unchanged.\n- [ ] `python scripts/check_complexity_baseline.py --check` and `python scripts/check_mechanism_delta.py --check` exit 0, and no `src/rebar` file exceeds 800 lines.\n- [ ] `env -u JIRA_URL -u JIRA_USER -u JIRA_API_TOKEN make verify` exits 0 on the commit pushed for review.","env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/reconciler/_backend.py","reason":"transport verbs"},{"path":"src/rebar/reconciler/adapters/jira/acli_graph.py","reason":"Cloud add/remove"},{"path":"src/rebar/reconciler/adapters/jira_datacenter/_issues.py","reason":"DC add/remove"},{"path":"src/rebar/reconciler/local_label_intent.py","reason":"release intent"},{"path":"src/rebar/reconciler/outbound_releases.py","reason":"new diff module"},{"path":"src/rebar/reconciler/outbound_differ.py","reason":"mutation and config fields"},{"path":"src/rebar/reconciler/outbound_mutation_builders.py","reason":"call diff"},{"path":"src/rebar/reconciler/outbound_pass.py","reason":"intent wiring"},{"path":"src/rebar/reconciler/mutation_payloads.py","reason":"outbound payload key"},{"path":"src/rebar/reconciler/dispatch_one.py","reason":"dispatch releases"},{"path":"src/rebar/reconciler/inbound_differ.py","reason":"same-pass suppression"},{"path":"docs/jira-sync-setup.md","reason":"outbound cell"},{"path":"tests/unit/reconciler/diffing/test_outbound_releases.py","reason":"new"},{"path":"tests/unit/reconciler/mutate/test_fix_version_transport.py","reason":"new"},{"path":"tests/unit/reconciler/mutate/test_local_label_intent.py","reason":"release intent"},{"path":"tests/unit/reconciler/test_field_contract_properties.py","reason":"intent gate"},{"path":"tests/integration/reconciler/test_reconcile_releases_roundtrip.py","reason":"new"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[["depends_on","50aa-b7a1-e9a1-44ac"],["parent","21ec-3e9b-4a27-4775"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"21ec-3e9b-4a27-4775","parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":[],"ticket_id":"59f4-6a6f-71e5-4084","ticket_type":"story","title":"Write rebar releases to Jira fixVersions with per-item add/remove (outbound)","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["dbc3eb68-9072-441b-9a8f-6407b96a369d","7049910d-7866-43ec-a945-b38d2e0aaee5","cbf22e23-2298-4d3d-adc0-816130ac80e7","b05d584d-ca72-4975-a9a8-b9ee519cb164"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1794264639989213002,"uuid":"fcf16c5c-a7e5-44bb-a441-c242420ce18c"}